er","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/date-picker#daterangepicker","content":"DateRangePicker"},"563":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-21","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/date-picker#datepickercalendar","content":"DatePickerCalendar"},"564":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-22","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/date-picker#daterangepickercalendar","content":"DateRangePickerCalendar"},"565":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-23","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/date-picker#datepickervalue","content":"DatePickerValue"},"566":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-24","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/date-picker#daterangepickervalue","content":"DateRangePickerValue"},"567":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-25","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#features","content":"**Composable interior**: Compose `Label`, a `Button slot=\"trigger\"`, `DatePickerCalendar`, and optional `Text` / `FieldError`. Nothing is added for you, and what you write keeps the order you wrote it in. `children` also accepts a function for picker state"},"568":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-26","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#features","content":"**Trigger and calendar**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders a calendar icon and the formatted value from the field. `DatePickerCalendar` (and `DateRangePickerCalendar`) opens a responsive calendar: it takes `Calendar` props plus `popoverProps` and `drawerProps` for its overlay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `Calendar` yourself to replace the whole overlay"},"569":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-27","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#features","content":"**Sizes**: Each picker is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets its label, trigger, description, error, and the calendar it opens; without it, the picker follows the surrounding scope"},"570":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-28","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#features","content":"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar"},"571":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-29","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#features","content":"Built on React Aria - native form integration, validation, focus management, and screen-reader support"},"572":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-30","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#features","content":"Label formatting via `formatOptions` / `placeholder` on the picker itself, or on `DatePickerValue` / `DateRangePickerValue` in a trigger you write"},"573":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-31","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#features","content":"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"},"574":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-32","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#working-with-dates","content":"Values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"},"575":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-33","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#working-with-dates","content":"Import date helpers from `@godaddy/antares/date` (a re-export of\n`@internationalized/date`).\nWrap the app in `<I18nProvider>` so formatting and the calendar follow the user's locale."},"576":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-34","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#default","content":"A single date picker with a `Label`."},"577":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-35","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#range","content":"A start/end range picker."},"578":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-36","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#controlled","content":"Driving the value with `useState`."},"579":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-37","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#mobile","content":"Below 40rem, the picker opens a scrolling drawer. Resize after closing to switch containers."},"580":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-38","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#format-options","content":"Controlling the trigger's label format via `formatOptions`."},"581":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-39","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#min--max","content":"Bounding selectable dates with `minValue` / `maxValue`."},"582":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-40","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#with-error","content":"An invalid picker showing a validation message via `isInvalid` and a `FieldError`."},"583":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-41","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#disabled","content":"A disabled picker via `isDisabled`."},"584":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-42","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#composed","content":"Write the trigger and the overlay yourself instead of composing `DatePickerCalendar`, for full\ncontrol over the popover and the calendar."},"585":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-43","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#composed-range","content":"Write a DateRangePicker's trigger and overlay from lower-level pieces the same way."},"586":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-44","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#sizes","content":"`size` sets the label, trigger, and calendar. Without it, the picker follows the surrounding\nsize scope."},"587":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-45","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#mobile-1","content":"Below `40rem`, `DatePickerCalendar` and `DateRangePickerCalendar` open a bottom drawer with vertically\nscrolling months. Each drawer page contains three months by default. Use Previous/Next to change pages,\nchoose a month, or type a year to jump directly. The initial date follows `focusedValue`,\n`defaultFocusedValue`, the selected date (range start), then today, constrained by the date bounds."},"588":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-46","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#mobile-1","content":"The overlay keeps its container until it closes, including during resizing. Its next opening uses the\ncurrent viewport. An initially open server-rendered picker keeps its popover through hydration."},"589":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-47","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#mobile-1","content":"Set `overlay=\"popover\"` on the calendar to always use the desktop presentation."},"590":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-48","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#mobile-1","content":"Use `drawerProps` for drawer presentation, such as `maxSize` or an accessible label. It defaults to\n`85dvh`. Open state stays on the picker; `popoverProps` configures the popover."},"591":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-49","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#mobile-1","content":"`pageCount` sets the number of months in either presentation. Defaults: three in the drawer, one in a\nsingle-date popover, and two in a range popover. Scrolling stays within the current page. Navigation\nadvances by a full page, or by one month with `pageBehavior=\"single\"`."},"592":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-50","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#mobile-1","content":"Range selection and endpoint dragging follow React Aria. Drawers default to `commitBehavior=\"reset\"`:\na calendar background press, focus leaving the calendar, or backdrop dismissal cancels a pending\nrange and preserves the previous value. Popovers default to `commitBehavior=\"select\"`, which commits\nthe pending range on background press or blur. Set `commitBehavior` on `DateRangePickerCalendar` to\noverride either default. Escape from a date cell cancels the pending selection."},"593":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-51","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#mobile-1","content":"`shouldCloseOnSelect={false}` on the picker keeps either presentation open after a selection."},"594":{"id":"/docs/components/date-picker-52","page_id":"/docs/components/date-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/date-picker#accessibility","content":"The drawer has the same accessible name as the picker. Escape, an outside press, or the screen-reader\ndismiss control closes it and returns focus to the trigger. Arrow keys and Page Up/Down retain React\nAria's calendar navigation. Scrolling does not move keyboard focus or change the selected value. The\nmonth/year controls follow the focused date, and each grid has its own month heading. Weekday\nlabels shorten when the calendar has limited space, including with enlarged text. The weekday row is\ndecorative; each date cell provides its full accessible name."},"595":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"page","content":"DropZone","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone"},"596":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-0","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone","content":"A standalone region that accepts drag-and-drop file interactions, rendering a clearly defined target area where users can drop files."},"597":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-1","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#installation","content":"Installation"},"598":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-2","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#examples","content":"Examples"},"599":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-3","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#default","content":"Default"},"600":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-4","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"601":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-5","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#file-upload","content":"File Upload"},"602":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-6","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#drop-target-label","content":"Drop Target Label"},"603":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-7","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#replace-existing-file","content":"Replace Existing File"},"604":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-8","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"605":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-9","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Keyboard"},"606":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-10","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"Screen readers"},"607":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-11","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"608":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-12","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#props","content":"Props"},"609":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-13","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#dropzone","content":"DropZone"},"610":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-14","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#default","content":"A minimal drop zone. The `onDrop` callback receives the dropped items; use the exported `isFileDropItem` guard to narrow them to files. Wrap the instructional text in `<Text slot=\"label\">` so it labels the visually hidden drop button for screen readers."},"611":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-15","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#disabled","content":"Set `isDisabled` to prevent the drop zone from accepting interactions. The zone is dimmed and the cursor indicates it is not interactive."},"612":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-16","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#file-upload","content":"A reference composition combining `DropZone` with `FileTrigger` to support both click-to-browse and drag-and-drop. Use this as a starting point and adapt the accepted formats, size limit, and handlers to your product's requirements."},"613":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-17","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#drop-target-label","content":"Pass a render-prop function as `children` to change the zone's content while a valid drag is active. Branching on `isDropTarget` requires no extra state. Pair it with `getDropOperation` to reject unsupported types - the label only appears when the drag is accepted."},"614":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-18","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#replace-existing-file","content":"Use `children` as a render function to show different content based on the current zone state - here, swapping the default label for \"Drop to replace\" when a file is already selected and a new drag is active. The same `onDrop` handler services both the drag path and the `FileTrigger` click path, so either gesture replaces the selection."},"615":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-19","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Key"},"616":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-20","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Description"},"617":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-21","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"`Tab`"},"618":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-22","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Moves focus to the drop zone"},"619":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-23","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"`Enter` / `Space`"},"620":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-24","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Opens the file picker so files can be selected without a pointer"},"621":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-25","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"The drop zone renders a visually hidden `<button>` inside the container. Assistive technology discovers and announces this button as an interactive element — activating it opens the native file picker without a pointer."},"622":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-26","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"The button's accessible name is built from two sources, combined in order:"},"623":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-27","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"**`<Text slot=\"label\">`** — any `Text` child with `slot=\"label\"` has its `id` linked to the button via `aria-labelledby`. This is the recommended way to provide a contextual label that is also visible to sighted users."},"624":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-28","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"**`aria-label`** — pass `aria-label` on the `DropZone` component to override or supplement the label (e.g. `aria-label=\"Upload profile photo\"`). When no `Text slot=\"label\"` is present and no `aria-label` is set, the button falls back to the default \"DropZone\" label provided by React Aria."},"625":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-29","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Use the drop zone alongside a button-based file picker — drag-and-drop is a convenience, never the only way to upload."},"626":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-30","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Replace the default text with `children` to communicate the accepted file types and size limits up front."},"627":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-31","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Let the drop zone fill its container; constrain it with the surrounding layout rather than setting a fixed width on the component itself."},"628":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-32","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Reflect upload state (validating, uploading, error) outside the drop zone so the target area stays clear and predictable."},"629":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","type":"page","content":"FieldError","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-error"},"630":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-0","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-error","content":"Validation message for a field. Renders only when the field is invalid."},"631":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-1","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-error#features","content":"Features"},"632":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-2","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-error#installation","content":"Installation"},"633":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-3","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-error#examples","content":"Examples"},"634":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-4","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-error#default","content":"Default"},"635":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-5","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-error#props","content":"Props"},"636":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-6","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-error#fielderror","content":"FieldError"},"637":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-7","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-error#features","content":"Shown when the parent field is invalid (`isInvalid` or native constraint validation)."},"638":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-8","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-error#default","content":"FieldError renders when the field is invalid."},"639":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"page","content":"FileTrigger","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger"},"640":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-0","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger","content":"A style-less primitive that wraps any pressable component and opens the native file picker when it is activated."},"641":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-1","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#features","content":"Features"},"642":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-2","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#installation","content":"Installation"},"643":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-3","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#examples","content":"Examples"},"644":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-4","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#default","content":"Default"},"645":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-5","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#accepted-types","content":"Accepted Types"},"646":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-6","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"647":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-7","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"648":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-8","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#props","content":"Props"},"649":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-9","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#filetrigger","content":"FileTrigger"},"650":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-10","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#features","content":"Turns any pressable component (such as an Antares `Button`) into a file picker trigger."},"651":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-11","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#features","content":"Renders a visually hidden `<input type=\"file\">` — no styling of its own."},"652":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-12","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#features","content":"Restricts selection by MIME type, allows multiple files, directory selection, and camera capture."},"653":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-13","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#features","content":"Resets the input value before every open, so re-selecting the same file still fires `onSelect`."},"654":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-14","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#default","content":"Wrap any pressable component. Activating the child opens the native file picker; the selected files arrive in `onSelect`."},"655":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-15","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#accepted-types","content":"Restrict the picker to specific MIME types with `acceptedFileTypes`, and allow more than one file with `allowsMultiple`."},"656":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-16","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#accessibility","content":"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."},"657":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-17","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#best-practices","content":"`acceptedFileTypes` is a best-effort filter for the OS picker — always validate file type and size again in your `onSelect` handler, since it can be bypassed."},"658":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-18","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#best-practices","content":"Pair `FileTrigger` with `DropZone` to offer both click-to-browse and drag-and-drop. See the DropZone \"File Upload\" example."},"659":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-19","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#best-practices","content":"Keep the child a single pressable element; `FileTrigger` forwards press behavior to whatever you nest inside it."},"660":{"id":"/docs/components/heading","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","type":"page","content":"Heading","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/heading"},"661":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-0","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/heading","content":"Semantic h1-h6 heading. Use slot=\"title\" inside a Modal or Dialog to name the overlay."},"662":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-1","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/heading#features","content":"Features"},"663":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-2","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/heading#installation","content":"Installation"},"664":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-3","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/heading#examples","content":"Examples"},"665":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-4","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/heading#default","content":"Default"},"666":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-5","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/heading#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"667":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-6","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/heading#props","content":"Props"},"668":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-7","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/heading#heading","content":"Heading"},"669":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-8","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/heading#features","content":"Renders `h1`-`h6` from the `level` prop (default `3`). The level never changes the visual size."},"670":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-9","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/heading#features","content":"Without `size`, takes the heading tier of the surrounding `SizeProvider`.\n`size` picks a step on the heading ramp (`xs` to `2xl`)."},"671":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-10","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/heading#features","content":"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."},"672":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-11","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/heading#features","content":"`slot=\"title\"` inside a `Modal` or `Dialog` sets the accessible name, and takes the overlay's\ntitle tier, one step above the heading tier."},"673":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-12","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/heading#default","content":"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."},"674":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-13","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/heading#sizes","content":"`level` sets the semantics and `size` sets the look, so the two never have to match. Without\n`size`, a heading takes the size scope's heading tier at any level."},"675":{"id":"/docs/components/icon","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","type":"page","content":"Icon","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/icon"},"676":{"id":"/docs/components/icon-0","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/icon","content":"Flexible SVG icon component with on-demand loading, automatic cachin