ble=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[2219,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[673,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[496,"`Icon slot=\"indicator\"` is decorative and receives `aria-hidden=\"true\"` automatically."],[832,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[861,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[2072,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[674,"`level` sets the semantics and `size` sets the look, so the two never have to match. Without\n`size`, a heading takes the size scope's heading tier at any level."],[2150,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[939,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[2149,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[906,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[203,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[573,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[995,"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."],[990,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[1186,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1947,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."],[1617,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1887,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[591,"`pageCount` sets the number of months in either presentation. Defaults: three in the drawer, one in a\nsingle-date popover, and two in a range popover. Scrolling stays within the current page. Navigation\nadvances by a full page, or by one month with `pageBehavior=\"single\"`."],[1071,"`PaginationDots` is decorative and does not replace interactive page\ncontrols."],[852,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[835,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[1091,"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."],[838,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[1125,"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."],[1130,"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."],[12